{"version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[]}],"results":[],"tool":{"driver":{"name":"Semgrep OSS","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The last user in the container is 'root'. This is a security hazard because if an attacker gains control of the container they will have root access. Switch back to another user after running commands as 'root'."},"help":{"markdown":"The last user in the container is 'root'. This is a security hazard because if an attacker gains control of the container they will have root access. Switch back to another user after running commands as 'root'.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint/wiki/DL3002)\n - [https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint/wiki/DL3002](https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint/wiki/DL3002)\n","text":"The last user in the container is 'root'. This is a security hazard because if an attacker gains control of the container they will have root access. Switch back to another user after running commands as 'root'."},"helpUri":"https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint/wiki/DL3002","id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.last-user-is-root","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.last-user-is-root","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["MEDIUM CONFIDENCE"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.last-user-is-root"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"By not specifying a USER, a program in the container may run as 'root'. This is a security hazard. If an attacker can control a process running as root, they may have control over the container. Ensure that the last USER in a Dockerfile is a USER other than 'root'."},"help":{"markdown":"By not specifying a USER, a program in the container may run as 'root'. This is a security hazard. If an attacker can control a process running as root, they may have control over the container. Ensure that the last USER in a Dockerfile is a USER other than 'root'.","text":"By not specifying a USER, a program in the container may run as 'root'. This is a security hazard. If an attacker can control a process running as root, they may have control over the container. Ensure that the last USER in a Dockerfile is a USER other than 'root'."},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.missing-user","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.missing-user","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["MEDIUM CONFIDENCE"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.missing-user"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Distroless base image not found. Please use `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian10` as a base image."},"help":{"markdown":"Distroless base image not found. Please use `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian10` as a base image.","text":"Distroless base image not found. Please use `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian10` as a base image."},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.use-distroless-base-image","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.use-distroless-base-image","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.dockerfile.use-distroless-base-image"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The 'Origin' header of the Websocket handshake request is not checked.\nThis could lead to Cross-Site WebSocket Hijacking vulnerability (CSWSH).\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The 'Origin' header of the Websocket handshake request is not checked.\nThis could lead to Cross-Site WebSocket Hijacking vulnerability (CSWSH).\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://christian-schneider.net/CrossSiteWebSocketHijacking.html](https://christian-schneider.net/CrossSiteWebSocketHijacking.html)\n","text":"The 'Origin' header of the Websocket handshake request is not checked.\nThis could lead to Cross-Site WebSocket Hijacking vulnerability (CSWSH).\n"},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.go.go.gorilla.security.audit.websocket-checkorigin-missing","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.go.go.gorilla.security.audit.websocket-checkorigin-missing","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-352","OWASP-A1: Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.go.go.gorilla.security.audit.websocket-checkorigin-missing"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected non-constant data passed into an LDAP query. If this data can be\ncontrolled by an external user, this is an LDAP injection.\nEnsure data passed to an LDAP query is not controllable; or properly sanitize\nthe data.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Detected non-constant data passed into an LDAP query. If this data can be\ncontrolled by an external user, this is an LDAP injection.\nEnsure data passed to an LDAP query is not controllable; or properly sanitize\nthe data.\n","text":"Detected non-constant data passed into an LDAP query. If this data can be\ncontrolled by an external user, this is an LDAP injection.\nEnsure data passed to an LDAP query is not controllable; or properly sanitize\nthe data.\n"},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.go.go.lang.security.ldap-injection.ldap-inection","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.go.go.lang.security.ldap-injection.ldap-inection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-90: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an LDAP Query ('LDAP Injection')","OWASP-A1: Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.go.go.lang.security.ldap-injection.ldap-inection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Generic XXE in `$JC`. The 'javax.xml.bind.Unmarshaller' parses XML and does not support any flags for disabling XXE, it's imperative\nto parse the untrusted XML through a configurable secure parser first, generate a source object as a result, and pass the\nsource object to the Unmarshaller.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Generic XXE in `$JC`. The 'javax.xml.bind.Unmarshaller' parses XML and does not support any flags for disabling XXE, it's imperative\nto parse the untrusted XML through a configurable secure parser first, generate a source object as a result, and pass the\nsource object to the Unmarshaller.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://github.com/OWASP/CheatSheetSeries/blob/master/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.md](https://github.com/OWASP/CheatSheetSeries/blob/master/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.md)\n","text":"Generic XXE in `$JC`. The 'javax.xml.bind.Unmarshaller' parses XML and does not support any flags for disabling XXE, it's imperative\nto parse the untrusted XML through a configurable secure parser first, generate a source object as a result, and pass the\nsource object to the Unmarshaller.\n"},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.XXE","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.XXE","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-611","OWASP-A4: XXE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.XXE"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible Lookup injection into Log4j messages.  \n"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible Lookup injection into Log4j messages.  \n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://www.lunasec.io/docs/blog/log4j-zero-day/)\n - [https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LOG4J2-3198](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LOG4J2-3198)\n - [https://www.lunasec.io/docs/blog/log4j-zero-day/](https://www.lunasec.io/docs/blog/log4j-zero-day/)\n - [https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/lookups.html](https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/lookups.html)\n","text":"Possible Lookup injection into Log4j messages.  \n"},"helpUri":"https://www.lunasec.io/docs/blog/log4j-zero-day/","id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.log4j-message-lookup-injection","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.log4j-message-lookup-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-74: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection')","OWASP-A1: Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.log4j-message-lookup-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The X-Forwarded-For (XFF) HTTP header field is a common method for identifying the originating\nIP address of a client connecting to a web server through an HTTP proxy or load balancer. Since this header \nis not set by server and can be easily spoofed by the client It may cause injection attacks if `$ADDR`\nis not filtered for properly.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The X-Forwarded-For (XFF) HTTP header field is a common method for identifying the originating\nIP address of a client connecting to a web server through an HTTP proxy or load balancer. Since this header \nis not set by server and can be easily spoofed by the client It may cause injection attacks if `$ADDR`\nis not filtered for properly.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Forwarded-For](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Forwarded-For)\n","text":"The X-Forwarded-For (XFF) HTTP header field is a common method for identifying the originating\nIP address of a client connecting to a web server through an HTTP proxy or load balancer. Since this header \nis not set by server and can be easily spoofed by the client It may cause injection attacks if `$ADDR`\nis not filtered for properly.\n"},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.x-forwarded-for","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.x-forwarded-for","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-20","OWASP-A1: Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.java.x-forwarded-for"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The software receives input from an upstream component that specifies multiple attributes, properties, or fields that are to be initialized or updated in an object, but it does not properly control which attributes can be modified.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The software receives input from an upstream component that specifies multiple attributes, properties, or fields that are to be initialized or updated in an object, but it does not properly control which attributes can be modified.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/915.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/915.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A8_2017-Insecure_Deserialization](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A8_2017-Insecure_Deserialization)\n - [https://sucuri.net/guides/owasp-top-10-security-vulnerabilities-2020/](https://sucuri.net/guides/owasp-top-10-security-vulnerabilities-2020/)\n","text":"The software receives input from an upstream component that specifies multiple attributes, properties, or fields that are to be initialized or updated in an object, but it does not properly control which attributes can be modified.\n"},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.php.lang.laravel.security.insecure-deserialization","name":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.php.lang.laravel.security.insecure-deserialization","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-502","OWASP-A8: Insecure Deserialization","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.php.lang.laravel.security.insecure-deserialization"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Without sufficient removal or quoting of SQL syntax in user-controllable inputs,\nthe generated SQL query can cause those inputs to be interpreted as SQL instead \nof ordinary user data. This can be used to alter query logic to bypass security checks,\nor to insert additional statements that modify the back-end database, possibly\nincluding execution of system commands.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Without sufficient removal or quoting of SQL syntax in user-controllable inputs,\nthe generated SQL query can cause those inputs to be interpreted as SQL instead \nof ordinary user data. This can be used to alter query logic to bypass security checks,\nor to insert additional statements that modify the back-end database, possibly\nincluding execution of system commands.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)\n","text":"Without sufficient removal or quoting of SQL syntax in user-controllable inputs,\nthe generated SQL query can cause those inputs to be interpreted as SQL instead \nof ordinary user data. This can be used to alter query logic to bypass security checks,\nor to insert additional statements that modify the back-end database, possibly\nincluding execution of system commands.\n"},"id":"security-scans.static_analysis_semgrep_2.repos.kondukto.php.lang.laravel